+  each outer-fold training prefix (635, 1268, 1901, 2534, and 3167 rows) for final
+  fitting, and separately on every nested inner-fold training prefix for tuning.
+- Each outer fold has five chronological inner folds contained entirely within
+  its training prefix. Each model family's parameters and the fold winner are
+  selected by inner mean MAE without access to the outer validation rows.
+- Fold-local selected features and parameters are used consistently by the
+  linear-regression baseline and every frozen tuned candidate.
+- Naive lag-1 remains a direct simple baseline and uses no feature selection.
+- No full-data refit, external holdout access, or locked-test access occurred.
+
